@startuml j3-booking-and-call-back
!include style.iuml
title J3 Booking and call-back
actor Patient
participant "Patient chat\n(index.html, chat.js,\ncallback-ask.js, sync.js)" as Chat
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core
database "Browser storage" as LS
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix
database "Store (Postgres)\nthrough api/_store.js" as Store
participant "Staff page\n(staff/index.html,\nstaff/staff.js, sync.js)" as SP
actor Staff
autonumber

Patient -> Chat : types "I want to book a check-up tomorrow at 5 pm" and presses Send
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(message, clinic file, language)
Core --> Chat : the booking reply with the time asked for, status "needs human"
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket (question, reply, requested time, call back)
Core -> LS : the ticket joins this browser's tickets
Chat --> Patient : "Thank you. I have passed your request for ... to our team";\nbelow it the form "So we can call you back (optional)"
Patient -> Chat : fills "Your name" and "Phone number" and presses Save
Chat -> Core : FD.updateTicket (name, phone with its country code)
Core -> LS : the ticket now holds the name and the number
Chat --> Patient : "Thank you, <name>. We will call <phone>."
Chat -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets (the ticket, with this browser's key)
Tix -> Store : the row in the table tickets is added, then updated
Staff -> SP : opens /staff and enters the desk code
SP -> Tix : sync.js: GET /api/tickets (with the desk code)
Tix --> SP : the tickets of every device
SP --> Staff : the ticket under "To call back" with the name, the phone and "requested <time>"
@enduml
